  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1247 PM CDT Mon Jun 22 2026\n\nThe upper level ridge is expected to remain over far West \nTX/northern Mexico over the next couple of days keeping high \ntemperatures at or near triple digits for the remainder of the week. \nEvening thunderstorms off the Caprock are possible Wednesday and \nThursday evening, though the existing ridge will mean activity is \nnot expected to be widespread with these northwest flow storms. This \nridge will begin to flatline Friday as a west coast trough gradually \ntakes its place Saturday, but precipitation chances should remain \nlow but uncertain during the weekend with hot and mostly sunny \nconditions persisting for much of the region.",
